## 2. Our preparation roadmap

1. Phase 1 – Java programming
   - OOP concepts
   - Classes and objects
   - Inheritance, polymorphism and abstraction
   - Interfaces and exception handling
   - Collections and multithreading
2. Phase 2 – Android fundamentals
   - Android architecture
   - Activities and Activity lifecycle
   - Intents and navigation
   - XML layouts and UI components
   - Permissions and background services
3. Phase 3 – Kotlin
   - Kotlin vs Java
   - Variables, functions and classes
   - Null safety
   - Data classes and extension functions
   - Coroutines and Flow
4. Phase 4 – Advanced Android
   - MVVM architecture
   - ViewModel and LiveData
   - Room database
   - Retrofit and API integration
   - Jetpack Navigation
5. Phase 5 – Maps and GPS
   - GPS and location tracking
   - Google Maps SDK
   - Markers and polylines
   - Geocoding and reverse geocoding
   - Navigation and route optimisation
6. Phase 6 – Practical development
   - Build a GPS-based Android application
   - Connect it to a REST API
   - Store trip history locally
   - Handle internet and location permissions
7. Phase 7 – Interview simulation
   - Java coding questions
   - Android technical questions
   - Project explanation
   - Scenario-based questions
   - HR questions and mock interview

